{"id":"basic-mathematics","version":1,"title":"Basic mathematics","subject":"Mathematics","level":"Secondary school","topic":"Everyday number skills","description":"Practice arithmetic, fractions, percentages, ratios and algebra.","estimatedMinutes":15,"language":"English + Nigerian Pidgin (demo review)","questions":[{"id":"math-01","text":"What is 25% of 80?","options":["10","20","25","40"],"answer":1,"topic":"Percentages","difficulty":"easy","explanation":{"english":{"short":"25% is one quarter, and one quarter of 80 is 20.","steps":["25% = 1/4.","80 divided by 4 is 20."]},"pidgin":{"short":"25% na one-quarter; one-quarter of 80 na 20.","steps":["25% mean one out of four.","Divide 80 by 4."]}}},{"id":"math-02","text":"Simplify 3/4 + 1/4.","options":["1/2","1","3/8","4/8"],"answer":1,"topic":"Fractions","difficulty":"easy","explanation":{"english":{"short":"The denominators match, so 4/4 equals 1.","steps":["Add 3 and 1.","Four quarters make one whole."]},"pidgin":{"short":"3 quarter plus 1 quarter na 4 quarter, and e equal 1.","steps":["Add the top numbers.","Four quarters make one whole."]}}},{"id":"math-03","text":"What is 7 x 8?","options":["48","54","56","64"],"answer":2,"topic":"Arithmetic","difficulty":"easy","explanation":{"english":{"short":"Seven groups of eight make 56.","steps":["8 x 5 = 40.","8 x 2 = 16, and 40 + 16 = 56."]},"pidgin":{"short":"7 times 8 na 56.","steps":["8 times 5 na 40.","Add 16 to get 56."]}}},{"id":"math-04","text":"Solve x + 6 = 14.","options":["6","8","20","-8"],"answer":1,"topic":"Algebra","difficulty":"easy","explanation":{"english":{"short":"Subtract 6 from both sides: x = 8.","steps":["Keep the equation balanced.","14 minus 6 equals 8."]},"pidgin":{"short":"Remove 6 from both sides; x go be 8.","steps":["Do the same thing each side.","14 minus 6 na 8."]}}},{"id":"math-05","text":"A ratio is 2:3. If the first part is 10, what is the second?","options":["12","15","20","30"],"answer":1,"topic":"Ratios","difficulty":"easy","explanation":{"english":{"short":"The scale factor is 5, so 3 x 5 = 15.","steps":["10 divided by 2 is 5.","Multiply the second ratio number by 5."]},"pidgin":{"short":"2 become 10 by factor 5, so 3 become 15.","steps":["Find the factor.","Use it for the second part."]}}},{"id":"math-06","text":"What is 0.6 as a fraction in simplest form?","options":["1/6","3/5","6/10","2/3"],"answer":1,"topic":"Fractions","difficulty":"easy","explanation":{"english":{"short":"0.6 = 6/10, which simplifies to 3/5.","steps":["Write six tenths.","Divide numerator and denominator by 2."]},"pidgin":{"short":"0.6 na 6/10, and simplify am to 3/5.","steps":["Write six over ten.","Divide both by two."]}}},{"id":"math-07","text":"What is 15% of 200?","options":["15","20","30","45"],"answer":2,"topic":"Percentages","difficulty":"easy","explanation":{"english":{"short":"10% of 200 is 20 and 5% is 10, giving 30.","steps":["Split 15% into 10% and 5%.","Add 20 and 10."]},"pidgin":{"short":"15% of 200 na 30.","steps":["10% give 20.","5% give 10; add them."]}}},{"id":"math-08","text":"If y = 4, what is 2y + 3?","options":["9","11","14","24"],"answer":1,"topic":"Algebra","difficulty":"easy","explanation":{"english":{"short":"Replace y with 4: 2(4) + 3 = 11.","steps":["Multiply 2 by 4.","Add 3 to get 11."]},"pidgin":{"short":"Put 4 where y dey: 8 plus 3 na 11.","steps":["Multiply 2 and 4.","Add 3."]}}},{"id":"math-09","text":"A book costs 500 naira and is reduced by 100 naira. New price?","options":["100","400","500","600"],"answer":1,"topic":"Arithmetic","difficulty":"easy","explanation":{"english":{"short":"Subtract the reduction: 500 - 100 = 400 naira.","steps":["Start with the original price.","Take away 100."]},"pidgin":{"short":"500 minus 100 na 400 naira.","steps":["Original price na 500.","Remove 100."]}}},{"id":"math-10","text":"Which is equivalent to 2:5?","options":["4:10","4:8","6:10","10:15"],"answer":0,"topic":"Ratios","difficulty":"easy","explanation":{"english":{"short":"Multiplying both parts by 2 gives 4:10.","steps":["A ratio stays equivalent when both terms use the same factor.","2 x 2 = 4 and 5 x 2 = 10."]},"pidgin":{"short":"Multiply both sides by 2: 2:5 become 4:10.","steps":["Use the same factor.","Both terms double."]}}}]}